+{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":328751,"duration_api_ms":331043,"ttft_ms":12674,"ttft_stream_ms":2920,"time_to_request_ms":343,"num_turns":7,"result":"I have everything I need: the contract, native fused semantics, the probe's exact checks, and the proven Dense004 CoreX closure-dispatch + native-Inductor-FP32 pattern. Here is the generated candidate.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plan\": [\n    \"Mirror Dense004's proven approach: reproduce the NATIVE torch.compile (Inductor) weighted-SwiGLU math exactly in Triton with FP32 interior arithmetic and single round-to-BF16 stores, so optimized stays inside atol 3e-4 / rtol 1e-3 against weighted_bias_swiglu_impl(input,None,weights,False) for output, input_grad AND weights_grad. No change to GEMMs, router, loss, dtype, dataset, baseline fusion, tolerance or timing.\",\n    \"Public entry weighted_swiglu(x, weights, *, native): fast path only for CUDA BF16 contiguous x[dim 2/3, even last dim] with BF16 contiguous weights[N,1] whose N == flattened token count; everything else (CPU, FP32, non-contiguous-incompatible, dtype/shape mismatch) delegates once, unchanged, through the supplied native callback passing the exact (x, weights) objects — satisfying the CPU/FP32 guard probes with zero native_fallback_calls on supported shapes.\",\n    \"Forward kernel (flattened over the H-sized output, H:tl.constexpr, BLOCK=1024, num_warps=4): a,b = BF16 gate/up loads .to(fp32); w = weights[row] load .to(fp32); sig = tl.sigmoid(a); y = ((a*sig)*b)*w; single BF16 store. This is exactly native swiglu(y)*weights then cast — one rounding. row=offs//H, col=offs%H, gate=row*2H+col, up=gate+H covers every even and odd H (257/769/2048).\",\n    \"Backward input_grad kernel on the SAME H-sized flattened grid: gg = g_fp32 * w_fp32 first (native swiglu_back(g*weights,y)); sig=tl.sigmoid(a); tmp8=gg*sig; tmp10=1-sig; tmp11=a*tmp10; tmp12=tmp11+1; tmp13=tmp8*tmp12; dx_gate=tmp13*b; dx_up=gg*(a*tl.sigmo