+{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":229065,"duration_api_ms":231282,"ttft_ms":6547,"ttft_stream_ms":3802,"time_to_request_ms":395,"num_turns":8,"result":"I have the full picture. Candidate003 caches fixed-grid runner closures keyed by exact `numel/N/grid`, so every new expert count misses and re-enters the vendor JIT launcher, whose key appends actual tensor `shape_info` → 220 recompiles. The fix is to cache the immutable `CompiledKernel` (bin) under a shape-independent key and, on hit, index it with the current grid and pass current tensors/`numel`, while marking the runtime size args `do_not_specialize` so one bin is valid across all N (and `N==1` isn't folded via `equal_to_1`).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plan\": [\n    \"Produce immutable candidate004 from candidate003 with identical arithmetic in all three kernels (forward elementwise weighted SwiGLU, input_grad two-halves store, wgrad native 2D [XBLOCK=1,RBLOCK=next_pow2(H)] FP32 accumulate then tl.sum(axis=1)[:,None]) and identical launch params (fwd/bwd BLOCK=1024 num_warps=4; wgrad XBLOCK=1 RBLOCK=next_power_of_2(H) num_warps=8 when RBLOCK>=2048 else 4 num_stages=1). Only the dispatch/caching changes; the frozen stage34 contract, gates, tolerances, native/control, seeds, timing and promotion rule are untouched.\",\n    \"Root cause confirmed in the vendor JIT launcher source: the compile/launch key ends with (..., use_sme, shape_info) and get_corex_sme returns empty shape_info for these pure elementwise/reduction kernels, so the launcher appends every tensor's actual .shape to shape_info. Candidate003 keys its own cache by exact (numel,N,grid), so each new expert token count is a fresh miss that re-enters kernel[grid](...), hits a fresh vendor shape_info key, and JIT-recompiles (220 compiles / 268 launcher_body in the untimed cProfile). do_not_specialize cannot remove shape_info; only bypassing the launcher on reuse does.\",\n    \"Fix: cache the IMMUTABLE CompiledKernel object (the bin returned by kernel[grid](...)) rather than a fixed-grid runner. First call for a key is a miss: kernel[grid](args, constexprs..., num_warps, num_stages, enable_sme=False) compiles once (going through the vendor launcher) and launches; store the returned bin. Every later call with the same key is a HIT: recompute the CURRENT grid (gx=ceil(numel/BLOCK) for fwd/bwd, (N,1,1) for wgrad) and launch via bin[(gx,1,1)](current runtime tensors + runtime numel/N), which runs CompiledKernel.c_wrapper directly, never recomputing the vendor key and never touching shape_info/JIT.\",\n    \"Make one bin valid across all N by marking the runtime size args do_not_specialize via supported string names (verified constructor normalizes str->regular_args.index): fwd/bwd kernels @triton.jit(do_not_specialize=[\\\"numel\\\"]) and wgrad @triton.jit(do_not_specialize=[\\\"xnumel\\\"]). This drops both the divisible-by-16 and the equal_to_1 specialization on those args, so a bin compiled at any token count (including a single-token N==1 expert, where xnumel would otherwise fold to constexpr 1) stays correct for every other count. H/TWO_H/XBLOCK/RBLOCK stay constexpr; numel/N stay regular runtime args still passed to the kernel.\",\n    \"Cache key reuses one bin only within an identical compiled-binary class and never forces shape-specific recompiles: key = (phase, device, dtype, H, BLOCK-or-RBLOCK, num_warps[, num_stages/XBLOCK], and every pointer data_ptr()%16). Pointers are NOT do_not_specialize, so their divisible-by-16 class is baked into the bin; including each pointer's %16 in the key guarantees we never reuse an aligned-compiled bin for an unaligned (offset-view) pointer. No exact numel/N/grid appears in the key because the arithmetic no longer needs it. For the contract (H=2048 fixed, fresh aligned allocations) this collapses to ~3 distinct keys / ~3 vendor compiles instead of one per expert count.\",\n    \"Pass enable_sme=False on every compile (miss) call: it is a documented vendor launcher kwarg (default True in the generated signature) and avoids compiler SME shape-dependent optimization for these pure elementwise/reduction kernels that contain no dot/GEMM. It does NOT remove the shape_info key (the bin-reuse bypass does that); at hit time enable_sme is irrelevant because bin[grid](...) skips the launcher entirely.\",\n    \"Keep a guarded reuse path with _state['closure_ok']: if bin[grid](...) ever raises on a hit (vendor runner rejecting the runtime args), flip closure_ok False, clear the cache, and from then on always take the correct plain kernel[grid](...) JIT path. This is a bin-reuse-unsupported guard only; there is NO hidden whole-operator fallback to native on supported shapes. The public entry weighted_swiglu keeps the exact candidate003 guard predicate (CUDA, BF16/BF16, x.dim() in (2,3), weights.dim()==2 last-dim-1, both contiguous, even last dim, weights.shape[0]==flattened rows) and delegates the whole call once to native only for genuinely unsupported inputs (CPU/FP32/non-contiguous/shape mismatch).\",\n    \"Preserve all boundary behavior: forward allocates a fresh (prefix,H) BF16 out and only launches when out.numel()!=0 (empty N0 skips kernels); backward does g=g.contiguous(), fresh dx=empty_like(x)/dw=empty_like(weights), launches input_grad then wgrad with N=numel//H only when g.numel()!=0. The wgrad loop uses rmask=rindex<H so tail widths H=257/769 mask correctly; masked other=0.0 keeps empty/odd widths safe within unchanged atol 3e-4/rtol 1e-3. Nothing cached is ever an output/input tensor, full pointer, or stream; the bin fetches the active stream per launch like native. Imports limited to torch, triton, triton.language; no env/file/network/seed/feedback/native-cache access and no hardcoded observed values.\",\n    \"Validation order is unchanged and not pre-judged: candidate004 must independently pass the 44-case probe + 2 actual offset views + 48 actual-native replays (bitwise) + the 3-step full-training comparisons (2627 checks / 1289 tensors) BEFORE any performance claim, then fresh full-MoE numerical admission, then the formal 9-process/120-step three-arm timing across seeds 34102/34103/34104 with first 20 discarded. Cross-shape bin reuse must pass those numerical gates with zero native fallbacks first. Compile counters will be checked in a separate untimed run; no speed/throughput gain is claimed until measured.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"The bin-reuse bypass (bin[(gx,1,1)](current args)) relies on vendor Triton 2.4.1 CompiledKernel.__getitem__ producing a runner that launches c_wrapper with current tensors, runtime numel/N and the live stream. Candidate003's equivalent runner-call path passed all 48 replays with zero fallbacks, so this is low-risk, but if a future vendor build changes the runner arity, closure_ok flips and every launch degrades to the correct-but-slower JIT path, so the >1% gain gate may not be met even though numerics are unaffected.\",\n    \"do_not_specialize must actually drop both divisible-by-16 and equal_to_1 for numel/xnumel in this vendor so a single bin is valid for N==1 through N==256; the constructor/launcher source shows specializations skip do_not_specialize indices and configs.equal_to_1 is derived from the same specialization, which supports this, but if the vendor still specialized xnumel==1 separately the single-token expert would need its own key (still correct, just an extra compile).\",\n    \"Pointer %16 is included in the key, but torch CUDA allocations are typically >=256-aligned so most keys collapse to %16==0; the 2 offset-view probes may land in a different alignment class and trigger one extra compile each. This cannot harm correctness, only cache-hit density.\",\n    \"Bitwise parity still depends on the vendor compiler lowering the copied [XBLOCK=1,RBLOCK] accumulate + tl.sum(axis=1)[:,None] to the identical FP32 reduction association as the original Inductor triton_red_fused_mul_silu_sum_1; this is inherited unchanged from candidate003 (which passed), but the bin is now reused across shapes, so if any shape-dependent codegen difference existed it would surface at the numerical gate.\",\n    \"enable_sme=False is passed only on the compile/miss call; if a vendor path ignored it and still emitted an SME shape-dependent binary, reusing that bin across N could in principle differ, though these kernels have no dot/GEMM/SME-eligible ops so the SME branch should be inert.\",\n    \"int32 offset arithmetic (TWO_H*x0 up to ~2.1M for N=256,H=2048) is safe for the declared moe-weighted contract shapes but would overflow for much larger inputs; candidate004 targets only the observed contract.\",\n    \"If a harness pins a stream around the module hook, the bin runner's per-launch stream fetch must be re-confirmed by the two fresh-input non-default-stream probes; no tolerance, timing, dtype or baseline-fusion weakening is introduced to compensate.\"\n  ],\n  \"code\": \"import torch\\nimport triton\\nimport triton.language as tl\\n\\n_BLOCK = 1024\\n_NUM_WARPS = 4\\n_launch_cache = {}\\n_state = {\\\"closure_ok\\\": True}\\n\\n\\n@triton.jit(do_not_specialize=[\\\"numel\\\"])\\ndef _wswiglu_fwd_kernel(x_ptr, w_ptr, y_ptr, numel, H: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\\n    pid = tl.program_id(0)\\n    offs = pid * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\\n    mask = offs < numel\\n    row = offs // H\\n    col = offs % H\\n    gate = row * (2 * H) + col\\n    up = gate + H\\n    a = tl.load(x_ptr + gate, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n    b = tl.load(x_ptr + up, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n    w = tl.load(w_ptr + row, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n    sig = tl.sigmoid(a)\\n    y = (a * sig) * b\\n    y = y * w\\n    tl.store(y_ptr + offs, y, mask=mask)\\n\\n\\n@triton.jit(do_not_specialize=[\\\"numel\\\"])\\ndef _wswiglu_bwd_input_kernel(x_ptr, g_ptr, w_ptr, dx_ptr, numel, H: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\\n    pid = tl.program_id(0)\\n    offs = pid * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\\n    mask = offs < numel\\n    row = offs // H\\n    col = offs % H\\n    gate = row * (2 * H) + col\\n    up = gate + H\\n    a = tl.load(x_ptr + gate, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n    b = tl.load(x_ptr + up, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n    g = tl.load(g_ptr + offs, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n    w = tl.load(w_ptr + row, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n    gg = g * w\\n    sig = tl.sigmoid(a)\\n    tmp8 = gg * sig\\n    tmp10 = 1 - sig\\n    tmp11 = a * tmp10\\n    tmp12 = tmp11 + 1\\n    tmp13 = tmp8 * tmp12\\n    dx_gate = tmp13 * b\\n    dx_up = gg * (a * tl.sigmoid(a))\\n    tl.store(dx_ptr + gate, dx_gate, mask=mask)\\n    tl.store(dx_ptr + up, dx_up, mask=mask)\\n\\n\\n@triton.jit(do_not_specialize=[\\\"xnumel\\\"])\\ndef _wswiglu_wgrad_kernel(in_ptr0, in_ptr1, out_ptr0, xnumel,\\n                          H: tl.constexpr, TWO_H: tl.constexpr,\\n                          XBLOCK: tl.constexpr, RBLOCK: tl.constexpr):\\n    xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\\n    xindex = xoffset + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK)[:, None]\\n    xmask = xindex < xnumel\\n    rbase = tl.arange(0, RBLOCK)[None, :]\\n    x0 = xindex\\n    _tmp10 = tl.full([XBLOCK, RBLOCK], 0, tl.float32)\\n    for roffset in range(0, H, RBLOCK):\\n        rindex = roffset + rbase\\n        rmask = rindex < H\\n        r1 = rindex\\n        tmp0 = tl.load(in_ptr0 + (r1 + (TWO_H * x0)), rmask & xmask, eviction_policy='evict_first', other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n        tmp5 = tl.load(in_ptr0 + (H + r1 + (TWO_H * x0)), rmask & xmask, eviction_policy='evict_first', other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n        tmp7 = tl.load(in_ptr1 + (r1 + (H * x0)), rmask & xmask, eviction_policy='evict_first', other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n        tmp1 = tmp0.to(tl.float32)\\n        tmp2 = tl.sigmoid(tmp1)\\n        tmp3 = tmp1 * tmp2\\n        tmp4 = tmp3.to(tl.float32)\\n        tmp6 = tmp4 * tmp5\\n        tmp8 = tmp6 * tmp7\\n        tmp9 = tl.broadcast_to(tmp8, [XBLOCK, RBLOCK])\\n        tmp11 = _tmp10 + tmp9\\n        _tmp10 = tl.where(rmask & xmask, tmp11, _tmp10)\\n    tmp10 = tl.sum(_tmp10, 1)[:, None]\\n    tl.store(out_ptr0 + (x0), tmp10, xmask)\\n\\n\\ndef _grid_x(numel):\\n    return (numel + _BLOCK - 1) // _BLOCK\\n\\n\\ndef _launch_fwd(x, w, out, numel, H):\\n    gx = _grid_x(numel)\\n    key = (\\\"fwd\\\", x.get_device(), x.dtype, H, _BLOCK, _NUM_WARPS,\\n           x.data_ptr() % 16, w.data_ptr() % 16, out.data_ptr() % 16)\\n    if _state[\\\"closure_ok\\\"]:\\n        binary = _launch_cache.get(key)\\n        if binary is not None:\\n            try:\\n                binary[(gx, 1, 1)](x, w, out, numel)\\n                return\\n            except Exception:\\n                _state[\\\"closure_ok\\\"] = False\\n                _launch_cache.clear()\\n    compiled = _wswiglu_fwd_kernel[(gx, 1, 1)](\\n        x, w, out, numel, H=H, BLOCK=_BLOCK, num_warps=_NUM_WARPS, enable_sme=False)\\n    if _state[\\\"closure_ok\\\"] and compiled is not None:\\n        _launch_cache[key] = compiled\\n\\n\\ndef _launch_bwd_input(x, g, w, dx, numel, H):\\n    gx = _grid_x(numel)\\n    key = (\\\"bwd_input\\\", x.get_device(), x.dtype, H, _BLOCK, _NUM_WARPS,\\n           x.data_ptr() % 16, g.data_ptr() % 16, w.data_ptr() % 16, dx.data_ptr() % 16)\\n    if _state[\\\"closure_ok\\\"]:\\n        binary = _launch_cache.get(key)\\n        if binary is not None:\\n            try:\\n                binary[(gx, 1, 1)](x, g, w, dx, numel)\\n                return\\n            except Exception:\\n                _state[\\\"closure_ok\\\"] = False\\n                _launch_cache.clear()\\n    compiled = _wswiglu_bwd_input_kernel[(gx, 1, 1)](\\n        x, g, w, dx, numel, H=H, BLOCK=_BLOCK, num_warps=_NUM_WARPS, enable_sme=False)\\n    if _state[\\\"closure_ok\\\"] and compiled is not None:\\n        _launch_cache[key] = compiled\\n\\n\\ndef _launch_wgrad(x, g, dw, N, H):\\n    rb = triton.next_power_of_2(H)\\n    nw = 8 if rb >=